<code>assert !c.isEmpty() => this.size() == c.size();</code>

However, to more accurately reflect the condition that the collection `c` is not null (as specified in the comment), we should also include a check for `c != null`. Since the constructor itself would throw a `NullPointerException` if `c` is null, the assertion should focus on the size equality when `c` is not null:

<code>assert c != null => this.size() == c.size();</code>
--------------------
<code>assert c != null => this.size() == c.size();</code>
--------------------
<code>assert c != null => this.size() == c.size();</code>
--------------------
